{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790888571,"nonce":"PAZATOXDPJwgjESkVzdPaF+9BKI=","title":"A vmalert configured as a source's Prometheus is reported as not answering, because vmalert serves no /api/v1/status/buildinfo","message":"**What is wrong.** The probe (`internal/sources/service/probe.go:233`) calls `BuildInfo` and on error records `WarnPrometheusUnreachable` — \"the paired Prometheus did not answer\". vmalert serves `/api/v1/rules` and `/api/v1/alerts` (`app/vmalert/web.go`) but not `/api/v1/status/buildinfo` (served by vmselect, not vmalert). `rule_name[]`, `type=alert` and `exclude_alerts` are all honoured by vmalert's `newRulesFilter`, so the rules path itself works.\n\n**The demonstration.** Pairing a source with `prometheus_url=http://vmalert:8880` shows the unreachable warning while RuleSnapshots resolve.\n\n**Why it matters.** A false health warning teaches operators to ignore the real one.\n\n**Where.** `probe.go`: when buildinfo fails, fall back to a minimal `GET /api/v1/rules?type=alert\u0026rule_name[]=\u003csentinel\u003e` and treat a valid envelope as reachable with version reported as unknown/`vmalert`; the warning message stops saying Prometheus when the server is not one.\n\n**Scope.** small.\n\n**Done when.** A vmalert-shaped fake answering rules but 404 on buildinfo probes as reachable; a server failing both still warns; Prometheus path unchanged.\n\n**Blocked by.** None — can start immediately.\n\n**Mode.** AFK — can be implemented and merged without a human decision. Source: ADR 0052/0053/0054 design session, 2026-10-02.","files":null}]}